# Types own behavior

Rust 1.98.1 / edition 2024 / resolver 3. New public API is a domain type with methods, not a module of `pub fn`. One type, real invariants. No `*Manager` / `*Service` / `*Util` pyramids, no DI.

## Owning type, not a free function

DO: `UidCrc::checked`, `SisField::bytes`, `SisUnsigned::bytes`, `SisController::field`, `SisPackage::package`.

DON'T: a new file of `pub fn foo(bytes: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8>` when a `struct Foo` exists or should. Don't add `encode_unsigned_sis`-style wrappers. If a thin free function already exists, the type method is canonical — do not add another wrapper, and do not mass-migrate `parse_mmp` / `encode_unsigned_sis` unless the task is that refactor.

Allowed free functions: a private algorithm with no owner (`epoc_crc16`), or an existing constructor that returns a type (`parse_mmp` → `Mmp`). New encode/parse for a type you are adding goes on that type.

```rust
// DON'T — new API as a free function, or Wine on the value type
pub fn encode_sis_controller(c: &SisController) -> Vec<u8> { ... }
impl UidCrc { pub fn wine_args(&self) -> Vec<String> { ... } }

// DO
impl SisEncode for SisController { const KIND: u32 = 13; fn payload(&self) -> Vec<u8> { ... } }
impl UidCrcTool { pub fn args(&self, crc: &UidCrc, outfile: Option<&str>) -> Vec<String> { ... } }
```

## Domain vs adapters

Value types (`UidCrc`, `SisField`, `SisUnsigned`, `SisUid`) never see Wine, EPOCROOT, argv, env, or process stdout. No `matches_wine` / `wine_args` on `UidCrc`.

Host I/O lives on `*Tool` / `*Backend`: `UidCrcTool::args`, `SisTools::from_env`, `Toolchain::from_env`.

## SisEncode, not copy-paste

Repeated KIND + payload + field is `SisEncode` (`const KIND`, `payload()`, default `field()`). Do not add `fn field()` helpers or a second encode trait. `SisField` and `SisUid` stay out of the trait.

## Re-exports

Crate-root `pub use` is append-only. `sis/mod.rs` `pub use` stays alphabetical. Add the new name; do not rewrite the block.
